This product includes software from craft-libs (https://github.com/storytold/craft-libs), licensed under the MIT License
or the Apache License 2.0, at your option. FilmCraft, PhotoCraft, EffectCraft and SoundCraft pull in its crates at their own
revisions. DiscCraft uses directly craft-audio (its AC-3 encoder, which makes the transcoded soundtracks Dolby Digital, and its
AC-3 decoder, with which a raw AC-3 file is heard in the monitor;
revision 6bfe8e7678dd470432b949154e78ec1f92fc64fc), craft-video (its H.264 encoder, formerly FilmCraft's
filmcraft-h264enc, which makes the HD Blu-ray video, and, only in a build with the transcode crate's `hevc` feature,
its HEVC encoder for Ultra HD video; the same revision; in tests also its MPEG-2 decoder), craft-media
(its MPEG-2 Systems, Matroska and MP4 readers, which take out video and audio that fit a disc as they are; the same
revision), craft-ui (its docking, which arranges the panels and workspaces, on the UI runtime the Crafting Apps share,
with craft-behavior's dock model, craft-host, craft-window and craft-theme; the same revision) craft-i18n (the
translation lookup the Crafting Apps share; the same revision), craft-menu with craft-keymap (the menu bar the
Crafting Apps share; the same revision), craft-captions (the caption files DiscCraft does not read itself: ASS / SSA,
SCC, MCC, EBU STL, TTML / DFXP, SAMI; the same revision), craft-mcp-server (the MCP server machinery the Crafting
Apps share, behind `disccraft-cli mcp`; the same revision), craft-sniff (an imported file's kind from its first
bytes; the same revision), craft-settings (the settings file, config.toml, as the Crafting Apps keep theirs; the
same revision), craft-dialogs (native file dialogs that never hold up a frame; the same
revision), craft-update (Help > Check for Updates...: finding, downloading and installing a newer release; the
same revision) and craft-fonts-build (embeds the craft-fonts faces a build is given, see below; the same revision),
and in tests
only craft-psd (PSD writer, the same revision) and craft-media-testkit with craft-testkit (where ffmpeg and ffprobe
are for the tests that compare with them; the same revision). craft-video and craft-media are taken from the fork https://github.com/mOqOm/craft-libs (branch
disccraft, under the same licences), which adds to that revision craft-libs pull requests #1992 and #2017 (H.264
field pictures and MBAFF) by their authors, stores that keep Matroska and MPEG-2 transport stream indexes between runs, and interlaced (1080i) H.264 encoding. Its vendored Hayro crates (with the vello and
linesweeper crates they draw with) are patched to revision 3eb5b528b08211844bc5c95c5a4fd169894d52ff in Cargo.toml.

